  "note": "A regional plan for any country in Region 3 without its own file here. National regulations come first, and allocations vary a lot: copy this file and edit it for your country. On VHF and UHF: A coarse regional plan: national regulations come first. 2 m is primary (146-148 MHz amateur only, no satellite). 70 and 23 cm are secondary, 70 cm is heavily used by ISM and unlicensed services, and 1260-1270 MHz satellites are Earth-to-space only. The plan has no FM or digital voice calling frequencies. Satellites using 144.0-144.025 MHz must stay above 144.0025 MHz. FT8 and MSK144 on 70 and 23 cm are WSJT-X defaults; the plan gives no centres of activity there. The non-amateur bands are only offered on a receiver, and a guide to what's where, not a statement of who may use it.",
